 locator('.progress-container')[22m\n    [2m    14 × locator resolved to <div class=\"progress-container mt-3 mb-4\">…</div>[22m\n    [2m       - unexpected value \"hidden\"[22m\n\n\n      68 |     if (!isVisible) {\n      69 |       console.log('Waiting for progress bar to appear...');\n    > 70 |       await expect(progressContainer).toBeVisible({ timeout: 10000 });\n         |                                       ^\n      71 |     }\n      72 |     console.log('Progress bar appeared');\n      73 |\n        at C:\\Users\\Raitis\\Desktop\\My WEB projects\\SEOIndicator-com\\Files-SEOIndicator-com\\tests\\indicator-checks.spec.js:70:39\n\n    attachment #1: screenshot (image/png) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n    local-test-results\\indicator-checks-Indicator-72b4f--indicator-with-AI-response-chromium\\test-failed-1.png\n    ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n    Error Context: local-test-results\\indicator-checks-Indicator-72b4f--indicator-with-AI-response-chromium\\error-context.md\n\n  1 failed\n    [chromium] › tests\\indicator-checks.spec.js:5:3 › Indicator Checks Test › should analyze raitisozols.com and verify URL indicator with AI response \n  4 passed (19.7s)\n\nTo open last HTML report run:\n[36m[39m\n[36m  npx playwright show-report[39m\n[36m[39m\nReport saved to: local-test-results\\index_12-02-2026_13-03-26.html\nRemoved .last-run.json file"}],"details":{"status":"failed","sessionId":"ember-ocean","total":83,"totalLines":83,"totalChars":3136,"truncated":false,"exitCode":1,"name":"npm test"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1770894227286}}
{"type":"message","id":"fca5ac0b","parentId":"e44cbfcb","timestamp":"2026-02-12T11:03:55.831Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Deciding test run scope**\n\nThe existing test suite has failures unrelated to the new homepage test, which passes locally when run in isolation. I'll run the new test locally to ensure it passes as required but note the unrelated existing failures. Next, I'll check deployment instructions.","thinkingSignature":"{\"encrypted_content\":\"\",\"id\":\"\",\"summary\":[{\"text\":\"**Deciding test run scope**\\n\\nThe existing test suite has failures unrelated to the new homepage test, which passes locally when run in isolation. I'll run the new test locally to ensure it passes as required but note the unrelated existing failures. Next, I'll check deployment instructions.\",\"type\":\"summary_text\"}],\"type\":\"reasoning\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_T1iJgbwgVwWCL4TwDrogzcbB|","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"C:\\Users\\Raitis\\Desktop\\My WEB projects\\SEOIndicator-com\\Files-SEOIndicator-com\\docs\\HOSTINGER-DEPLOYMENT-SETUP.md"},"partialJson":"{\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\Raitis\\\\Desktop\\\\My WEB projects\\\\SEOIndicator-com\\\\Files-SEOIndicator-com\\\\docs\\\\HOSTINGER-DEPLOYMENT-SETUP.md\"}"}],"api":"openai-responses","provider":"github-copilot","model":"gpt-5.2-codex","usage":{"input":1652,"output":314,"cacheRead":9856,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":11822,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1770894227288}}
{"type":"message","id":"222aabf9","parentId":"fca5ac0b","timestamp":"2026-02-12T11:03:55.856Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_T1iJgbwgVwWCL4TwDrogzcbB|","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Hostinger Automated Deployment Setup\r\n\r\nThis guide explains how to set up automated deployment from GitHub Actions to your Hostinger shared hosting account.\r\n\r\n## 🎯 **What This Provides**\r\n\r\n- ✅ **Automatic deployment** on every push to main branch\r\n- ✅ **Production testing** after deployment\r\n- ✅ **Failed test logs** for debugging\r\n- ✅ **Secure FTP deployment** to Hostinger\r\n- ✅ **File filtering** (excludes development files)\r\n\r\n## 🔧 **Setup Instructions**\r\n\r\n### 1. Get Hostinger FTP Credentials\r\n\r\n1. **Login to Hostinger Control Panel**\r\n2. **Go to File Manager** or **FTP Accounts**\r\n3. **Note down these details:**\r\n   - FTP Host (usually: `ftp.yourdomain.com` or IP address)\r\n   - FTP Username (usually: `yourdomain.com` or custom)\r\n   - FTP Password\r\n\r\n### 2. Add GitHub Secrets\r\n\r\n1. **Go to your GitHub repository**\r\n2. **Click Settings** → **Secrets and variables** → **Actions**\r\n3. **Add these repository secrets:**\r\n\r\n```\r\nHOSTINGER_FTP_HOST = ftp.yourdomain.com\r\nHOSTINGER_FTP_USERNAME = yourdomain.com\r\nHOSTINGER_FTP_PASSWORD = your_ftp_password\r\n```\r\n\r\n### 3. File Structure on Hostinger\r\n\r\nYour files will be deployed to `/public_html/` directory:\r\n\r\n```\r\npublic_html/\r\n├── index.php\r\n├── style.css\r\n├── api/\r\n├── seo-guides/\r\n├── config.php\r\n├── db_config.php\r\n└── ... (other PHP files)\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Excluded files** (won't be deployed):\r\n- `.git/` and `.github/`\r\n- `node_modules/`\r\n- `tests/` and `test-logs/`\r\n- `package.json` and `playwright.config.js`\r\n- Development files\r\n\r\n## 🚀 **Workflow Overview**\r\n\r\n### **Deploy and Test Workflow** (`.github/workflows/deploy-and-test.yml`)\r\n\r\n1. **Deploy Phase:**\r\n   - Checkout code\r\n   - Install dependencies\r\n   - Deploy to Hostinger via FTP\r\n   - Wait for deployment propagation\r\n\r\n2. **Test Phase:**\r\n   - Install Playwright browsers\r\n   - Run tests against production site\r\n   - Generate failure logs if tests fail\r\n   - Commit logs to repository\r\n\r\n### **Separate Test Workflow** (`.github/workflows/playwright.yml`)\r\n\r\n- Runs tests against production site\r\n- No deployment (for testing only)\r\n- Useful for testing without deploying\r\n\r\n## 📋 **Deployment Process**\r\n\r\n### **Automatic Deployment:**\r\n```bash\r\ngit add .\r\ngit commit -m \"Update website\"\r\ngit push origin main\r\n```\r\n\r\n**What happens:**\r\n1. ✅ **Code deploys** to Hostinger\r\n2. ✅ **Tests run** against production\r\n3. ✅ **Success/ failure** reported in GitHub Actions\r\n4. ✅ **Logs created** if tests fail\r\n\r\n### **Manual Deployment:**\r\n- Go to **Actions** tab in GitHub\r\n- Click **Deploy and Test Production**\r\n- Click **Run workflow**\r\n\r\n## 🔒 **Security Features**\r\n\r\n- ✅ **FTP credentials** stored as encrypted secrets\r\n- ✅ **No sensitive files** deployed (config.php, .env)\r\n- ✅ **Development files** excluded\r\n- ✅ **Secure SFTP** connection\r\n\r\n## 🐛 **Troubleshooting**\r\n\r\n### **Deployment Fails:**\r\n1. **Check FTP credentials** in GitHub secrets\r\n2. **Verify FTP host** is correct\r\n3. **Check Hostinger** file permissions\r\n4. **Review deployment logs** in GitHub Actions\r\n\r\n### **Tests Fail After Deployment:**\r\n1. **Check production site** manually: https://seoindicator.com\r\n2. **Review test logs** in `test-logs/` directory\r\n3. **Verify file upload** was successful\r\n4. **Check for PHP errors** in Hostinger logs\r\n\r\n### **Site Not Accessible:**\r\n1. **Check file permissions** on Hostinger\r\n2. **Verify index.php** was uploaded\r\n3. **Check .htaccess** file (if any)\r\n4. **Review Hostinger** error logs\r\n\r\n## 📊 **Monitoring**\r\n\r\n### **Success Indicators:**\r\n- ✅ **Green checkmark** in GitHub Actions\r\n- ✅ **Site accessible** at https://seoindicator.com\r\n- ✅ **Tests passing** in production\r\n\r\n### **Failure Indicators:**\r\n- ❌ **Red X** in GitHub Actions\r\n- ❌ **Failed test logs** in repository\r\n- ❌ **Site not accessible** or errors\r\n\r\n## 🎉 **Benefits**\r\n\r\n- ✅ **Zero-downtime deployment** (files upload directly)\r\n- ✅ **Automatic testing** after deployment\r\n- ✅ **Version control** integration\r\n- ✅ **Rollback capability** (git revert)\r\n- ✅ **Team collaboration** (multiple developers)\r\n- ✅ **Production monitoring** (automated tests)\r\n\r\n## 🔄 **Workflow Customization**\r\n\r\n### **Change Deployment Branch:**\r\nEdit `.github/workflows/deploy-and-test.yml`:\r\n```yaml\r\non:\r\n  push:\r\n    branches: [ main, develop ]  # Add your branches\r\n```\r\n\r\n### **Exclude More Files:**\r\nAdd to the `exclude` section:\r\n```yaml\r\nexclude: |\r\n  **/.git*\r\n  **/your-custom-file.txt\r\n  **/temp/**\r\n```\r\n\r\n### **Add Build Step:**\r\nIf you need to build assets:\r\n```yaml\r\n- name: Build assets\r\n  run: |\r\n    npm run build\r\n    # Add your build commands\r\n```\r\n\r\n## 📞 **Support**\r\n\r\nIf you encounter issues:\r\n1. **Check GitHub Actions logs** for detailed error messages\r\n2. **Verify Hostinger** FTP settings\r\n3. **Test FTP connection** manually\r\n4. **Review this guide** for common solutions\r\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1770894235854}}
{"type":"message","id":"92316612","parentId":"222aabf9","timestamp":"2026-02-12T11:04:01.658Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Confirming manual deploy trigger need**\n\nAuto-deploy on push is disabled, so deployment requires manually running the workflow, likely via GitHub UI or CLI; next step is to examine the GitHub workflow files for precise deploy instructions and possible local scripts or tools.","thinkingSignature":"{\"encrypted_content\":\"\",\"id\":\"\",\"summary\":[{\"text\":\"**Confirming manual deploy trigger need**\\n\\nAuto-deploy on push is disabled, so deployment requires manually running the workflow, likely via GitHub UI or CLI; next step is to examine the GitHub workflow files for precise deploy instructions and possible local scripts or tools.\",\"type\":\"summary_text\"}],\"type\":\"reasoning\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_ekSqPtOMYXAqcTMeIwcyp8zP|","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"C:\\Users\\Raitis\\Desktop\\My WEB projects\\SEOIndicator-com\\Files-SEOIndicator-com\\.github\\workflows\\deploy-and-test.yml"},"partialJson":"{\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\Raitis\\\\Desktop\\\\My WEB projects\\\\SEOIndicator-com\\\\Files-SEOIndicator-com\\\\.github\\\\workflows\\\\deploy-and-test.yml\"}"}],"api":"openai-responses","provider":"github-copilot","model":"gpt-5.2-codex","usage":{"input":5233,"output":248,"cacheRead":7808,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":13289,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1770894235857}}
{"type":"message","id":"9a3f7e7f","parentId":"92316612","timestamp":"2026-02-12T11:04:01.684Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_ekSqPtOMYXAqcTMeIwcyp8zP|","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"name: Deploy and Test Production\r\n\r\non:\r\n  workflow_dispatch:\r\n\r\njobs:\r\n  deploy:\r\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\r\n    permissions:\r\n      contents: write\r\n    outputs:\r\n      deployed: ${{ steps.deploy.outcome == 'success' }}\r\n    \r\n    steps:\r\n    - name: Checkout code\r\n      uses: actions/checkout@v4\r\n    \r\n    - name: Setup Node.js\r\n      uses: actions/setup-node@v4\r\n      with:\r\n        node-version: lts/*\r\n        cache: 'npm'\r\n    \r\n    - name: Disable man-db triggers for faster apt operations\r\n      run: |\r\n        echo \"set man-db/auto-update false\" | sudo debconf-communicate\r\n        sudo dpkg-reconfigure man-db\r\n    \r\n    - name: Install dependencies\r\n      run: npm ci --prefer-offline --no-audit --no-fund\r\n    \r\n    - name: Deploy to Hostinger\r\n      id: deploy\r\n      uses: SamKirkland/FTP-Deploy-Action@v4.3.4\r\n      with:\r\n        server: ${{ secrets.HOSTINGER_FTP_HOST }}\r\n        username: ${{ secrets.HOSTINGER_FTP_USERNAME }}\r\n        password: ${{ secrets.HOSTINGER_FTP_PASSWORD }}\r\n        server-dir: /public_html/\r\n        exclude: |\r\n          **/.git*\r\n          **/.git*/**\r\n          **/node_modules/**\r\n          **/.github/**\r\n          **/tests/**\r\n          **/prod-test-results/**\r\n          **/local-test-results/**\r\n          **/ci-test-results/**\r\n          **/playwright-report/**\r\n          **/.env\r\n          **/config.php\r\n          **/db_config.php\r\n          **/package.json\r\n          **/package-lock.json\r\n          **/playwright.config.js\r\n          **/CI-SETUP.md\r\n          **/README.md\r\n          **/to_do.txt\r\n          **/to_fix.txt\r\n          **/project_overview.txt\r\n    \r\n    - name: Wait for deployment\r\n      run: sleep 15  # Reduced wait time for faster execution\r\n\r\n  test-production:\r\n    needs: deploy\r\n    if: needs.deploy.outputs.deployed == 'true'\r\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\r\n    timeout-minutes: 15\r\n    permissions:\r\n      contents: write\r\n    \r\n    steps:\r\n    - name: Checkout code\r\n      uses: actions/checkout@v4\r\n    \r\n    - name: Setup Node.js\r\n      uses: actions/setup-node@v4\r\n      with:\r\n        node-version: lts/*\r\n        cache: 'npm'\r\n    \r\n    - name: Disable man-db triggers for faster apt operations\r\n      run: |\r\n        echo \"set man-db/auto-update false\" | sudo debconf-communicate\r\n        sudo dpkg-reconfigure man-db\r\n    \r\n    - name: Install dependencies\r\n      run: npm ci --prefer-offline --no-audit --no-fund\r\n    \r\n    - name: Cache Playwright browsers\r\n      uses: actions/cache@v4\r\n      id: playwright-cache\r\n      with:\r\n        path: |\r\n          ~/.cache/ms-playwright\r\n        key: playwright-chrome-${{ hashFiles('package-lock.json') }}\r\n        restore-keys: |\r\n          playwright-chrome-\r\n          playwright-browsers-\r\n    \r\n    - name: Install Playwright Browsers\r\n      if: steps.playwright-cache.outputs.cache-hit != 'true'\r\n      run: npx playwright install --with-deps chrome\r\n    \r\n    - name: Run Production Tests\r\n      run: |\r\n        npx playwright test --max-failures=1 --workers=2 --reporter=github 2>&1 | tee test-output.log\r\n        exit ${PIPESTATUS[0]}\r\n    \r\n    - name: Generate Failed Tests Log\r\n      if: failure()\r\n      run: |\r\n        echo \"# Production Test Failure Report - $(date)\" > failed-tests.md\r\n        echo \"\" >> failed-tests.md\r\n        echo \"## Deployment & Test Summary\" >> failed-tests.md\r\n        echo \"- **Date**: $(date)\" >> failed-tests.md\r\n        echo \"- **Commit**: ${{ github.sha }}\" >> failed-tests.md\r\n        echo \"- **Branch**: ${{ github.ref_name }}\" >> failed-tests.md\r\n        echo \"- **Deployed to**: https://seoindicator.com\" >> failed-tests.md\r\n        echo \"- **Test Environment**: Production\" >> failed-tests.md\r\n        echo \"\" >> failed-tests.md\r\n        echo \"## Test Output\" >> failed-tests.md\r\n        echo \"\" >> failed-tests.md\r\n        \r\n        if [ -f \"test-output.log\" ]; then\r\n          echo \"### Console Output\" >> failed-tests.md\r\n          echo '```' >> failed-tests.md\r\n          tail -50 test-output.log >> failed-tests.md\r\n          echo '```' >> failed-tests.md\r\n          echo \"\" >> failed-tests.md\r\n        fi\r\n        \r\n        echo \"### Environment Information\" >> failed-tests.md\r\n        echo \"- **OS**: $(uname -a)\" >> failed-tests.md\r\n        echo \"- **Node Version**: $(node --version)\" >> failed-tests.md\r\n        echo \"- **Playwright Version**: $(npx playwright --version)\" >> failed-tests.md\r\n        echo \"- **Browser**: Chrome (stable channel)\" >> failed-tests.md\r\n        echo \"- **Target URL**: https://seoindicator.com\" >> failed-tests.md\r\n        echo \"\" >> failed-tests.md\r\n        \r\n        echo \"## Next Steps\" >> failed-tests.md\r\n        echo \"1. Check the production site: https://seoindicator.com\" >> failed-tests.md\r\n        echo \"2. Review test failures and fix issues\" >> failed-tests.md\r\n        echo \"3. Re-run tests after fixes\" >> failed-tests.md\r\n        echo \"4. Check deployment logs if site is not accessible\" >> failed-tests.md\r\n    \r\n    - name: Upload Failed Tests Log\r\n      if: failure()\r\n      uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4\r\n      with:\r\n        name: production-test-failure\r\n        path: failed-tests.md\r\n        retention-days: 30\r\n    \r\n    - name: Commit Failed Test Log to Repository\r\n      if: failure()\r\n      run: |\r\n        if [ -f \"failed-tests.md\" ]; then\r\n          TIMESTAMP=$(date +\"%Y%m%d_%H%M%S\")\r\n          COMMIT_SHORT=$(echo \"${{ github.sha }}\" | cut -c1-7)\r\n          FILENAME=\"prod-test-results/production_failed_tests_${TIMESTAMP}_${COMMIT_SHORT}.md\"\r\n          \r\n          mkdir -p prod-test-results\r\n          mv failed-tests.md \"$FILENAME\"\r\n          \r\n          {\r\n            echo \"# Production Test Failure Report\"\r\n            echo \"\"\r\n            echo \"**Workflow Run**: [${{ github.server_url }}/${{ github.repository }}/actions/runs/${{ github.run_id }}](${{ github.server_url }}/${{ github.repository }}/actions/runs/${{ github.run_id }})\"\r\n            echo \"**Commit**: [${{ github.sha }}](${{ github.server_url }}/${{ github.repository }}/commit/${{ github.sha }})\"\r\n            echo \"**Branch**: ${{ github.ref_name }}\"\r\n            echo \"**Deployed to**: https://seoindicator.com\"\r\n            echo \"**Date**: $(date)\"\r\n            echo \"\"\r\n            echo \"---\"\r\n            echo \"\"\r\n            cat \"$FILENAME\"\r\n          } > \"$FILENAME.tmp\" && mv \"$FILENAME.tmp\" \"$FILENAME\"\r\n          \r\n          git config --local user.email \"action@github.com\"\r\n          git config --local user.name \"GitHub Action\"\r\n          \r\n          git add \"$FILENAME\"\r\n          git commit -m \"Add production test failure log from workflow run ${{ github.run_id }}\" || echo \"No changes to commit\"\r\n          \r\n          git push origin HEAD:${{ github.ref_name }} || echo \"Failed to push changes\"\r\n        fi\r\n    \r\n    - name: Upload Playwright Report\r\n      if: always()\r\n      uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4\r\n      with:\r\n        name: production-playwright-report\r\n        path: playwright-report/\r\n        retention-days: 30\r\n        if-no-files-found: ignore\r\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1770894241681}}
